Subject: Cantor Current Evidence Manifest Rehash Repair Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 2f5f73d5-7be7-4a57-b25a-ff747a45d670
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Current_Evidence_Manifest_Rehash_Repair.sop

& [Problem] is measured
  + VerifyOnly reports 58 stale artifact records across 23 current manifests and 1030 references
  + the full workspace gate stops at candidate workspace evidence because README.md metadata is stale
  + the standing fault identifies dependency-first topological metadata regeneration as the repair

& [SelectedSolution] is least authority
  + reuse the existing dependency-aware rehasher whose historical role is artifact-only refresh
  + read current files and update only recorded byte length, SHA-256, and existing generated time
  + preserve frozen evidence and never invoke evidence-producing builders or probes

& [RejectedAlternatives] remain outside authority
  + hand editing only README records would miss transitive and unrelated stale references
  + rerunning candidate, topology, provider, benchmark, or workspace probes would create new evidence and exceed the repair purpose
  + ignoring the fault would leave the global gate knowingly red
  + deleting manifests or weakening tests would destroy evidence rather than repair it

& [Decision] is authorize one bounded metadata-only rehash after phase lock
